@startuml Use Item (Heal) - Communication Diagram
!theme plain
title **UC-4: Use Item (Heal) – Communication Diagram**

object ":GameView" as ui #LightBlue
object ":GameController" as ctrl #LightGreen
object ":EatAction" as ea #LightYellow
object ":HealEffect" as he #Orange
object ":Hero" as hero #Pink
object ":Inventory" as inv #Wheat
object ":Consumable" as cons #Plum
object ":GameSession" as sess #White

ui -- ctrl
ctrl -- ea
ctrl -- he
ctrl -- sess
ea -- sess
ea -- hero
ea -- inv
ea -- cons
ea -- he
he -- hero
hero -- inv

ui -> ctrl : 1: executeAction(eatAction)
ctrl -> ea : 1.1: <<create>> EatAction(consumable)
ctrl -> ea : 1.2: resolve(session)
ea -> sess : 1.2.1: getHero()
ea -> hero : 1.2.2: getInventory()
ea -> inv : 1.2.3: removeItem(consumable)
ea -> cons : 1.2.4: getHealAmount()
ea -> he : 1.2.5: <<create>> HealEffect(hero, healAmount)
ctrl -> he : 1.3: apply(session)
he -> hero : 1.3.1: heal(healAmount)
ctrl -> sess : 1.4: advanceTurn()

note bottom of ctrl
  **GRASP Controller**: GameController coordinates.
  **Creator**: Controller creates EatAction (has consumable ref).
  EatAction creates HealEffect (Information Expert –
  it knows the consumable's heal amount).
  **Information Expert**: Inventory.removeItem() manages
  its own contents; Hero.heal() manages its own HP.
end note

@enduml
